# Skill: Taste Evaluation

Purpose:
  Evaluate design quality and aesthetic coherence. Detect "slop" —
  generic AI-generated design fingerprints — and enforce project-specific
  taste boundaries.

Owns: design/taste-evaluation.sdd
ID: DESIGN-TASTE-EVALUATION

Domain: design

Level: L3

Status: STABLE

Use:
  - Design quality audits
  - Anti-slop enforcement
  - Aesthetic family validation
  - Brand consistency checks

Input:
  - DESIGN.md or design system tokens
  - UI implementation (code/screenshot)
  - Aesthetic family definition

Output:
  - Taste score (0-100)
  - Slop detection report
  - Aesthetic consistency metrics
  - Remediation recommendations

Execute:
  1. Load project DESIGN.md and aesthetic family
  2. Extract design tokens: color, typography, spacing, radius, shadow
  3. Compare implementation against declared tokens
  4. Run slop detection heuristics:
     - Overused gradients
     - Generic Inter/Roboto font stacking
     - Purple-blue gradient defaults
     - Card-heavy layout without variation
     - Emoji in headers/CTAs
  5. Calculate taste score
  6. Produce remediation plan

Taste Heuristics:
  - Typography: <= 2 font families; display + body pairing intentional
  - Color: palette <= 5 primary colors; contrast ratio >= 4.5:1
  - Spacing: consistent 8px grid; no magic numbers
  - Motion: transitions <= 300ms; easing intentional
  - Imagery: custom or styled; no generic stock photos
  - Voice: no emoji in titles; no "revolutionary" / "seamless" copy

Anti-Slop Kit:
  - Avoid: purple gradients, glassmorphism everywhere, rounded-3xl cards
  - Avoid: Inter as sole typeface, 14px body text everywhere
  - Avoid: hero section with gradient + 3 cards + testimonial
  - Prefer: intentional restraint, custom details, brand-specific motifs

Validation:
  - Score >= 70: PASS
  - Score 50-69: WARN
  - Score < 50: BLOCK

Avoid:
  - Generic AI-generated landing pages
  - Overused component patterns without customization
  - Ignoring project brand guidelines

State: +
